event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":92,"item_id":"rs_07964a67cd4fba7f016acd262d965087d198bf195a308e9782","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Addressing newline handling**\n\nI'm focusing on preserving the leading newline in a textarea since the parser seems to strip the first one. It looks like I need to use a specific HTML entity to keep it intact. This has to do with how the standard tokenizer manages line breaks. I should prepend a newline and escape the saved text to ensure the first one is removed after processing. Additionally, I’m noting some chunk handling for Unicode as a separate bug fix to consider later."}

