data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":793,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_07964a67cd4fba7f016acd262bf80087d1a0791923d2c504e5","object":"response","created_at":1791829548,"completed_at":1791829567,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_07964a67cd4fba7f016acd262d965087d198bf195a308e9782","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Addressing newline handling**\n\nI'm focusing on preserving the leading newline in a textarea since the parser seems to strip the first one. It looks like I need to use a specific HTML entity to keep it intact. This has to do with how the standard tokenizer manages line breaks. I should prepend a newline and escape the saved text to ensure the first one is removed after processing. Additionally, I’m noting some chunk handling for Unicode as a separate bug fix to consider later."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqzSYzuj2l2nVv8aMtf36uW66eGouFTPQSoV5IPR_KoD5SLq11mmxM8I2ilx1OAJbu0oW5ACiclyr7UOQh8_Z2Wf10KL7Ur1xqkeotFhjCbP05NFzua5U9GFhKkQDtxF6wSPOTM3yz2rJfntkoZ8FfuhsGp4qzdDJdTusavFbTEhNHTmUXv1-gVHQNniOP_NOeRrmq3HetMHLE-ag8PDI7Zr2nTBVxqiuGv3D4yl7czoHXS00sWThPbP99W2xshaszmU9mwAa23peIO63XBwuN4r3I80Kd7DB1tfEhhwYh2IsZPbq7IpHHA0oqmOjkpAtgInO3m9M8nowM0AESL_-vGpmHAE42jdglgKPcM_JqJopvw2XiIubNBROcb6xE2MsPSHFakRJG3UQSNpE-9Wi2wmyTcZrk5VS_grYhva3D2ykoGRKs3t92XceUx1X2hDT-ZYC7HL14r4qnpi7e6MamSX6ZmUSMhRhpEsVCxbSdSw-OWlp2Q9FYywVh8G-LC_F-SVNeD_Wod9sZ-d3iDnXJ_tdBF7xR0cEgnEwBgHhojGZN1InlbqfbP6jkLEnybQUr0ayJAeXFm4zYPxUHf2HKvrJr1stzI7wt4S3EmCeRs-ftE4dKDudwxh6AV1cAD8wMoJP5erqDhDdW4RyNuBPOvvKJg9cvfon5FqmQaE_6ByUINZw2QVmhvXO2urAxFVEtvUu6uDrx6K4JoGXMWZTCb8jyKQkya3_T2heVFeoBXPPJy28-vL0phx18Fq-vdf1uc6VIZCKz8PsMYwZLXNXWkUFGgpcycuyrn2Kd_0jMYgpZpr_QljRvzsxYFrX3qSeUcqYUNkGHMM1emeLVqY3ZYPK8IxSVRfV4SxbYBVpMd3Lh-0v6N_p9MhPuVS9cN-V8ikscMxkyiCbHikWXSGuNsGQfBqNGvBYwfmnnNeSN4ji_UBi1631QC7uhAGpKAlkH3n6BR-SW6q3CY-xoSsb3kElP7Xq-gu3PZ-YBhGI_n5YcOfe_e7GZnNruS1AIYzp77_aLSk7t8HfjDMYKLrMML7G1rIXMOxICE5Pxhrb0sksxvHcyfHsHH1HE9cBxhnwxPrqKKGNQuYtWl3w6_AEZGm9plJ8CDZlCzX96vpSSM-B-e077PsssQ96Krfzl2X-nzUr10_iE9DFWdNg5Q7XLa1YCQpRK_frQahiAXCMEMQg6GSQ4U0VeQmI8gOUs6ta75ycu7UDe7laFMZ_12axbOPf4A0TE2g4O5B_7cEJ7FZlQY-HIzalT_-njnHDxdTQ0v8zbGvZ4N0_VDuvR4GPIA7ouvM3UsGcoh_2lvfZ2lSsUn28i11gVFTb4g-_dV3UKrEt5XSRLqIjt_XTLZkOrOnbOqn42_oa0HxLScE_6Ictn0JsOQhxTSwJ38Y7QSB0A5dg0yV14dPsOQuJb56PEbcMcJywFcg6JWRsS-GqtTuxQg4wjz_cGCPzSAltQkuHDMQ98qDBZ9bZyS4Sw5HwxiYpGUCNOCE_acLzpfDY8ZCJ6tvzLjqqn9klrydIX2NJhxL3_mDiAhFYia_IPWRjKWeOwjmmYk1jwgKBZtwfONJsPc9JFd1aYSUZK99RbzOWTx31UdL1DBTGkMB3tlUk1dwkBgkakFF-Rg8nK_2XepsFS7rKZbkPMLg5uAkYhCltLMUMPvIX9BIkcmVzGy5JG2UIowmItb8ni-vco_FYrMupTbpUjL2rz8wB2x7uCeCR2oZuXglTffV2kiChYiRwwRsxDYXZJJj_r32S85vGf2psV8H2tS8rVif7heDsIAu-ckG4RPgkAP9QYC4oonnXyT2UjvT2Fp38MNmP-9bgIBhObjfIR_0SedMAAkozDtqSgC3NciOj1MTyHx2GAFm410K7dC_S2kg4SNJk83YZR2mWBLleFxfYm1Lkgn8vX3DxSLCM4S